From ad4e255ce4bb4cbb925213ee71d8f3a1e004b89e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:43:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Describe a door with GPT, Claude, or Gemini for the door
 editor's comparison tool.

Server-side generation for the AI door-description comparison. One admin-only
procedure, aiDoorDescription.describeWithAi, sends a column's own prompt and the
door's sample photo to that column's provider and returns the description text.
Provider keys stay on the server: OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, and
GEMINI_API_KEY are read here and never returned or bundled.

A missing key answers { status: "not-connected" } with the plain sentence the
column shows, so the button says "Claude isn't connected yet" instead of failing
silently. The prompt is capped and only the three known models are accepted, so
the endpoint cannot be used as a general-purpose model proxy.

Shared with the frontend: shared/aiDoorPrompts.ts (the same prompts the UI shows)
and shared/aiDoorDescribe.ts (the contract).
